---
layout: base.njk
permalink: /editor/
noindex: true
# A noindex page has no business in the sitemap.
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
pageTitle: Profile editor
pageDescription: Local editing tool for this profile. Not profile content.
pageStyles: /assets/editor.css
pageScript: /assets/editor.js
---

{#
  Every section is a fieldset whose legend is a toggle button: the grouping
  stays semantic, the body collapses, and which sections are open is remembered
  in this browser. The chevron is inline rather than a background image so it
  can turn with the button's aria-expanded state.
#}

{% macro sectionHead(id, label, icon, counts) %}
<legend>
  <button type="button" class="section-toggle" data-section-toggle="{{ id }}"
          aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="section-{{ id }}">
    <svg class="chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
         stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
      <path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"/>
    </svg>
    {% if icon %}<i class="fa-solid {{ icon }}" style="margin-right: 0.5rem; color: var(--accent);"></i>{% endif %}
    {{ label | safe }}
    {% if counts %}<span class="section-count" data-section-count="{{ id }}"></span>{% endif %}
  </button>
</legend>
{% endmacro %}


{#
  The row of controls above a repeatable list: how many entries it holds, and —
  for the lists with dates on them — a one-click way back to newest-first after
  dragging. Rendered here so the markup stays in the template, filled by the script.
#}
{% macro listTools(id, addLabel, dated) %}
<div class="list-tools">
  <p class="list-count muted" data-list-count="{{ id }}" aria-live="polite"></p>
  <span class="toolbar-spacer"></span>
  {#- Collapses the rows of this list only. The toolbar's Collapse all works on
      whole sections; this one is for the drop-downs inside one of them. It
      hides itself below two rows, where a row's own title is enough. -#}
  <button type="button" class="btn btn-small" data-rows-toggle="{{ id }}" hidden><i class="fa-solid fa-compress" style="margin-right: 0.3rem;"></i>Collapse all</button>
  {% if dated %}
  <button type="button" class="btn btn-small" data-sort="{{ id }}"><i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-down-short-wide" style="margin-right: 0.3rem;"></i>Sort by date</button>
  {% endif %}
  <button type="button" class="btn btn-small" data-add="{{ id }}"><i class="fa-solid fa-plus" style="margin-right: 0.3rem;"></i>{{ addLabel }}</button>
</div>
{% endmacro %}

<div class="editor" data-editor>
  <header class="editor-intro">
    <h1>Profile</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Everything the platform knows about you lives here: Search scores jobs against it, CVs &amp; CLs
      write from it, and applications are filled in from it. Type it in, or upload your documents and
      let the AI propose the entries for you to approve.
    </p>
    <p class="muted" data-mode-note>Checking how this page is running…</p>
    <details class="editor-intro-help">
      <summary>How this editor works</summary>
      <p class="muted">
        Fields marked <span class="required">required</span> have no fallback in the published profile,
        so <strong>Save profile</strong> and <strong>Download .json</strong> check them before they run.
        Everything else is optional.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">
        Every section heading and every entry inside one opens and closes when you click it. Which
        sections you left open is remembered in this browser, and a closed section is still saved.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">
        <strong>The order you put things in is the order they are published.</strong> Drag a row by its
        handle (<span class="grip-inline" aria-hidden="true">⠿</span>) to move it, or focus the handle
        and press <kbd>↑</kbd>/<kbd>↓</kbd>. <strong>Sort by date</strong> puts a list back in
        newest-first order.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">
        What you type is kept in this browser as you go, so a refresh loses nothing. On your own
        computer, <strong>Save profile</strong> writes it to <code>data/</code> (what the public site
        shows) and to <code>src/assets/Student-data/student.json</code> (the private copy, with what is
        never published). <a href="{{ '/' | url }}?public">See your public profile</a>.
      </p>
    </details>
    {# Rows move without anything visible changing for a screen reader, so every
       move says where the row landed. #}
    <p class="visually-hidden" data-reorder-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
  </header>

  <div class="editor-toolbar" role="group" aria-label="Save and export">
    <span class="save-status" data-save-status aria-live="polite">Loading…</span>
    <span class="toolbar-spacer"></span>
    <button type="button" class="btn" data-action="toggle-all" aria-live="polite"><i class="fa-solid fa-compress" style="margin-right: 0.3rem;"></i>Collapse all</button>
    <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" data-action="save-server" hidden><i class="fa-solid fa-floppy-disk" style="margin-right: 0.3rem;"></i>Save profile</button>
    <button type="button" class="btn" data-action="export"><i class="fa-solid fa-download" style="margin-right: 0.3rem;"></i>Download .json</button>
    <button type="button" class="btn" data-action="import"><i class="fa-solid fa-upload" style="margin-right: 0.3rem;"></i>Load .json</button>
    <button type="button" class="btn btn-danger" data-action="reset"><i class="fa-solid fa-trash-can" style="margin-right: 0.3rem;"></i>Clear all</button>
    <input type="file" accept="application/json,.json" data-import-input hidden>
  </div>

  <ul class="data-summary" data-summary aria-label="What is loaded"></ul>

  <form class="editor-form" data-form autocomplete="on">
    {# Shown only on your own computer: the documents stay in src/assets/Student-data/documents and are never published. #}
    <fieldset class="collapsible" data-documents hidden>
      {{ sectionHead("documents", "Import from your documents", "fa-wand-magic-sparkles", true) }}
      <div class="section-body" id="section-documents">
        <p class="muted">
          Upload certificates, course and internship certificates, employment references, transcripts,
          project documents or an old CV. The AI reads each one and proposes profile entries.
          <strong>Nothing is added until you review it and tick it</strong>, and every value says
          whether it was found in the document, came from online research on the provider, or is
          only the AI's suggestion.
        </p>
        <label class="dropzone" data-documents-drop>
          <i class="fa-solid fa-cloud-arrow-up dropzone-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          <span class="dropzone-label">Upload documents</span>
          <span class="dropzone-text">Drop PDF, picture, Word or text files here, or click to choose. Up to 20 MB each.</span>
          <input type="file" accept=".pdf,.png,.jpg,.jpeg,.webp,.docx,.txt,.md" multiple data-documents-input>
        </label>
        <p class="muted" data-documents-note></p>
        <div class="doc-list" data-documents-list aria-live="polite"></div>
      </div>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset class="collapsible">
      {{ sectionHead("student-data", "Base CV &amp; cover letter", "fa-file-invoice", true) }}
      <div class="section-body" id="section-student-data">
        <p class="muted">The two documents the tailoring starts from. They are kept in <code>src/assets/Student-data/</code> on this computer and never published.</p>
                  <div class="grid-2">
            <div class="dropzone" data-dropzone>
  <i class="fa-solid fa-cloud-arrow-up dropzone-icon"></i>
  <span class="dropzone-label">Base CV (EN)</span>
  <span class="dropzone-text">Drag & drop .pdf or .docx here, or click to browse</span>
  <div class="dropzone-info">
    <span class="current-doc" data-doc-display="base_cv_en"></span>
    <span class="dropzone-file-name" data-file-name="base_cv_en"></span>
  </div>
  <input type="file" accept=".pdf,.docx" data-doc-upload="base_cv_en">
</div>
            <div class="dropzone" data-dropzone>
  <i class="fa-solid fa-cloud-arrow-up dropzone-icon"></i>
  <span class="dropzone-label">Base Cover Letter (EN)</span>
  <span class="dropzone-text">Drag & drop .pdf or .docx here, or click to browse</span>
  <div class="dropzone-info">
    <span class="current-doc" data-doc-display="base_cover_letter_en"></span>
    <span class="dropzone-file-name" data-file-name="base_cover_letter_en"></span>
  </div>
  <input type="file" accept=".pdf,.docx" data-doc-upload="base_cover_letter_en">
</div>
          </div>
      </div>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset class="collapsible">
      {{ sectionHead("basics", "Basics", "fa-user") }}
      <div class="section-body" id="section-basics">
        <div class="grid-2">
          <label>First name <span class="required">required</span>
            <input type="text" data-path="profile.firstName" autocomplete="given-name" required>
          </label>
          <label>Last name <span class="required">required</span>
            <input type="text" data-path="profile.lastName" autocomplete="family-name" required>
          </label>
        </div>
        <label>Headline <span class="required">required</span>
          <textarea rows="3" data-path="profile.headline"
            placeholder="Cloud Infrastructure Engineer" required></textarea>
          <small>Sits under your name. Line breaks are kept, so you can run it over more than one line.</small>
        </label>
        <div class="grid-2">
          <label>Location <span class="optional">optional</span>
            <input type="text" data-path="profile.location" placeholder="Amman, Jordan">
            <small>Leave blank to publish no location.</small>
          </label>
          <label>Pronouns <span class="optional">optional</span>
            <select data-path="profile.pronouns">
              <option value="">Not specified</option>
              <option value="he/him">he/him</option>
              <option value="she/her">she/her</option>
            </select>
            <small>Leave as Not specified to publish no pronouns at all.</small>
          </label>
        </div>
        <label>Email
          <input type="email" data-path="profile.email" autocomplete="email" placeholder="you@example.com">
          <small>Published in the HTML, the JSON-LD and /llms.txt. Leave blank to publish no email.</small>
        </label>
        <label>Phone <span class="optional">optional</span>
          <input type="tel" data-private-phone autocomplete="tel" placeholder="+49 170 0000000" maxlength="30" disabled>
          <small data-private-phone-note>Private: saved to the gitignored <code>data/profile-private.json</code> and never published. Needs <code>npm run editor</code>.</small>
        </label>

        <h3 class="subhead">Languages</h3>
        <p class="muted">
          Every language you can work in professionally, with your honest level. This is not
          decoration: the <strong>Language Gate</strong> that <code>/apply</code> and
          <code>/rank</code> run treats an undeclared language as a hard no rather than a gap
          to talk around, so leave out what you do not actually work in — and add what you do,
          or German-language postings cannot be scored at all.
        </p>
        <div data-list="languages" class="entry-editor-list"></div>
        {{ listTools("languages", "Add language", false) }}
      </div>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset class="collapsible">
      {{ sectionHead("about", "About", "fa-address-card") }}
      <div class="section-body" id="section-about">
        <label>About me <span class="required">required</span>
          <textarea rows="7" data-path="profile.bio" required
            placeholder="Two to four sentences. Write it the way you would want an AI assistant to summarize you to someone else."></textarea>
          <small>The single most-quoted piece of text when an assistant summarizes you. State facts, not marketing.</small>
        </label>
      </div>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset class="collapsible">
      {{ sectionHead("education", "Education &amp; academic qualifications", "fa-graduation-cap", true) }}
      <div class="section-body" id="section-education">
        <div data-list="education" class="entry-editor-list"></div>
        {{ listTools("education", "Add education", true) }}
      </div>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset class="collapsible">
      {{ sectionHead("experience", "Work experience &amp; internships", "fa-briefcase", true) }}
      <div class="section-body" id="section-experience">
        <div data-list="experience" class="entry-editor-list"></div>
        {{ listTools("experience", "Add position", true) }}
      </div>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset class="collapsible">
      {{ sectionHead("projects", "Projects", "fa-lightbulb", true) }}
      <div class="section-body" id="section-projects">
        <p class="muted">
          Work you can point at that no employer owns: a side project, a university
          capstone, an open-source contribution. Published to <code>data/projects.json</code>,
          to <code>/llms.txt</code>, and as the <em>Independent Projects</em> section of the
          profile the job-search commands read.
        </p>
        <div data-list="projects" class="entry-editor-list"></div>
        {{ listTools("projects", "Add project", true) }}
      </div>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset class="collapsible">
      {{ sectionHead("certificates", "Licenses &amp; certifications", "fa-certificate", true) }}
      <div class="section-body" id="section-certificates">
        <div data-list="certificates" class="entry-editor-list"></div>
        {{ listTools("certificates", "Add certification", true) }}
      </div>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset class="collapsible">
      {{ sectionHead("courses", "Courses &amp; training", "fa-chalkboard-user", true) }}
      <div class="section-body" id="section-courses">
        <p class="muted">Courses you completed that are not a formal certification: a university module worth naming, an online course, a workshop.</p>
        <div data-list="courses" class="entry-editor-list"></div>
        {{ listTools("courses", "Add course", true) }}
      </div>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset class="collapsible">
      {{ sectionHead("awards", "Achievements", "fa-trophy", true) }}
      <div class="section-body" id="section-awards">
        <p class="muted">Prizes, scholarships, rankings and anything else you earned that a recruiter can check.</p>
        <div data-list="awards" class="entry-editor-list"></div>
        {{ listTools("awards", "Add achievement", true) }}
      </div>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset class="collapsible">
      {{ sectionHead("links", "Links", "fa-link", true) }}
      <div class="section-body" id="section-links">
        <div data-list="links" class="entry-editor-list"></div>
        {{ listTools("links", "Add link", false) }}
      </div>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset class="collapsible">
      {{ sectionHead("radar", "Skills radar", "fa-chart-pie") }}
      <div class="section-body" id="section-radar">
        <p class="muted">
          Your skills by field, from every role, project, certificate and extra skill. Skills you have
          pasted from job adverts (<strong>From a job ad</strong>) show as a second shape, so the gap
          between what employers ask and what you can show is visible.
        </p>
        <div id="skills-radar" class="skills-radar" role="img" aria-label="Radar chart of your skills by field"></div>
        <div class="radar-ai">
          <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" data-action="analyse-skills" disabled><i class="fa-solid fa-wand-magic-sparkles" style="margin-right: 0.3rem;"></i>Analyse with AI</button>
          <button type="button" class="btn" data-action="radar-reset" hidden>Back to my skills</button>
          <span class="muted" data-radar-ai-note>Needs <code>npm run editor</code> and an AI provider (set in the workspace).</span>
        </div>
        <div class="radar-notes" data-radar-notes aria-live="polite"></div>
      </div>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset class="collapsible">
      {{ sectionHead("skills", "Technical skills", "fa-star", true) }}
      <div class="section-body" id="section-skills">
        <p class="muted">
          Skills that no role, project or certificate already covers. The site unions these
          with every skill listed on a position, a project or a certification.
        </p>
        <p class="muted">
          Every skills box takes a whole list at once — paste one skill per line, or
          comma-separated. <strong><i class="fa-solid fa-list-check"></i> Add skills</strong> browses a catalogue by field and
          searches it, German labels included. <strong>From a job ad</strong> takes a pasted
          advert and pulls the skills out of it. The type-ahead offers your own skills first,
          then ones it has seen in adverts, then the catalogue — and anything you type is
          accepted whether or not it has heard of it. Duplicates are dropped whatever their
          capitalisation.
        </p>
        <div data-skills="profile.skills"></div>
      </div>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset class="collapsible">
      {{ sectionHead("soft", "Soft skills &amp; professional interests", "fa-people-group") }}
      <div class="section-body" id="section-soft">
        <h3 class="subhead">Soft skills</h3>
        <p class="muted">How you work: the ones you can back with an example from a role or a project above. Used in cover letters, never to pass a requirement you do not meet.</p>
        <div data-skills="extras.softSkills"></div>
        <h3 class="subhead">Professional interests</h3>
        <p class="muted">The fields and kinds of work you want. They steer which postings rank first.</p>
        <div data-skills="extras.interests"></div>
      </div>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset class="collapsible">
      {{ sectionHead("availability", "Availability &amp; constraints", "fa-calendar-check") }}
      <div class="section-body" id="section-availability">
        <label>Current status <span class="optional">optional</span>
          <input type="text" data-path="extras.employmentStatus" placeholder="Final-year student, exchange semester in Germany">
          <small>One line. Application forms ask for it.</small>
        </label>
        <label>Constraints <span class="optional">optional</span>
          <textarea rows="3" data-path="extras.constraints" placeholder="Available from March 2027 for 6 months, full time. Residence permit until September 2027."></textarea>
          <small>Dates, hours, permits, relocation. Form answers are written from this and nothing is assumed beyond it.</small>
        </label>
      </div>
    </fieldset>
  </form>

  <section class="editor-help">
    <h2>What happens to this data</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing here is uploaded anywhere by the page itself. Text is stored in this browser's
      <code>localStorage</code> and images in its <code>IndexedDB</code>, both private to
      this browser on this device.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Download .json</strong> gives you one file containing everything, images
      included. To publish it, run <code>npm run import-data -- &lt;file&gt;</code> in the
      repository, then commit and push — the site rebuilds from it. Documents you upload stay
      in <code>src/assets/Student-data/documents</code> on your computer.
    </p>
    <p data-local-help hidden>
      Because you are running <code>npm run editor</code>, <strong>Save profile</strong> is
      available and skips the download entirely: it writes
      <code>data/profile.json</code>, <code>data/experience.json</code>,
      <code>data/projects.json</code>, <code>data/certificates.json</code> and the images
      straight into the repository.
    </p>
  </section>
</div>

<script src="{{ '/assets/thinking-orbs.js' | url }}"></script>
<script src="{{ '/assets/ai-status.js' | url }}"></script>
